---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout 
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="Important safety and legal disclaimers for The Driveway Mechanic website and automotive DIY content."
  noIndex={true}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-foreground mb-8">Disclaimer</h1>
    
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-2xl border border-red-500/30 bg-gradient-to-br from-red-500/10 to-transparent p-8">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-red-600 text-white shrink-0">
            <svg class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-red-700 dark:text-red-400 mb-2">Important Safety Notice</h2>
            <p class="text-red-600 dark:text-red-300">
              Working on vehicles can be dangerous. This website provides information for educational purposes only. 
              You assume all risks and responsibility for any work performed on your vehicle.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Use of Information</h2>
      <p>
        The Driveway Mechanic website provides automotive information and guidance for educational and informational 
        purposes only. While we strive to provide accurate and up-to-date information, we make no representations 
        or warranties of any kind, express or implied, about the completeness, accuracy, reliability, suitability, 
        or availability of the information, products, services, or related graphics contained on this website.
      </p>

      <h2>Safety and Risk</h2>
      <p>
        Automotive repair and maintenance work can be inherently dangerous. Activities described on this website 
        may involve:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Working with hazardous materials and chemicals</li>
        <li>Operating power tools and equipment</li>
        <li>Working under vehicles that must be properly supported</li>
        <li>Electrical systems that can cause injury or death</li>
        <li>High-pressure systems and hot components</li>
      </ul>
      
      <p>
        <strong>You assume all risk and responsibility for your safety</strong> when following any information, 
        instructions, or procedures outlined on this website.
      </p>

      <h2>Professional Consultation</h2>
      <p>
        Always consult with qualified automotive professionals when:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>You are unsure about any procedure or diagnosis</li>
        <li>Working on safety-critical systems (brakes, steering, airbags)</li>
        <li>The repair involves structural components</li>
        <li>You lack the proper tools or experience</li>
        <li>Your vehicle is under warranty</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Vehicle Variations</h2>
      <p>
        Information provided may not apply to all vehicle makes, models, or years. Always consult your vehicle's 
        owner's manual and service procedures for your specific vehicle before attempting any work.
      </p>

      <h2>No Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Under no circumstances shall The Driveway Mechanic, its authors, or contributors be liable for any 
        direct, indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages resulting from the use or inability 
        to use the information provided on this website, including but not limited to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Personal injury or death</li>
        <li>Property damage</li>
        <li>Vehicle damage</li>
        <li>Financial loss</li>
        <li>Loss of use of vehicle</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Affiliate Links</h2>
      <p>
        This website contains affiliate links to products and services. We may receive a commission if you 
        purchase through these links at no additional cost to you. This does not influence our recommendations, 
        which are based on our honest assessment of products.
      </p>

      <h2>Information Accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        While we make every effort to provide accurate information, automotive technology and procedures 
        change frequently. Information may become outdated or may not apply to your specific situation. 
        Always verify information through multiple sources and consult current technical documentation.
      </p>

      <h2>Independent Contractor Status</h2>
      <p>
        The Driveway Mechanic is not affiliated with any automotive manufacturer, dealer, or repair facility. 
        Recommendations and opinions expressed are independent and based on our assessment.
      </p>

      <h2>Modification of Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        This disclaimer may be modified at any time without notice. Continued use of this website constitutes 
        acceptance of any changes to this disclaimer.
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg font-semibold mt-8">
        Remember: When in doubt, prioritize safety over savings. There's no shame in consulting a professional 
        when you're uncertain about any repair or maintenance procedure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>